WEBVTT

cue-1
00:00:00.379 --> 00:00:04.999
From the schedule and assessment setting
page, go to the assessment settings tab.

cue-2
00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:11.480
Here, you will see a list of scored
activities. You can manage them one by one

cue-3
00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:12.460
or in bulk.

cue-4
00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:16.040
Let's look at settings for individual
assessments first.

cue-5
00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:22.319
Each activity includes multiple settings
you can adjust regarding when and how

cue-6
00:00:22.319 --> 00:00:28.379
students experience it. To do so, simply
click and select or enter your changes.

cue-7
00:00:29.099 --> 00:00:33.959
To mention a few tips, the time of date
here follows the 24-hour system.

cue-8
00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:40.299
Enabling targeted retake mode will allow
students to only redo questions they got

cue-9
00:00:40.299 --> 00:00:46.380
wrong. Also, passwords and exceptions will
help set special access rules or

cue-10
00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:51.680
accommodations for individual students.
You can also use the search bar to search

cue-11
00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:58.039
for specific assessment names. Now, let's
look into the bulk apply function. With

cue-12
00:00:58.039 --> 00:01:03.740
many assessments, managing one by one can
be tedious. Bulk apply allows you to copy

cue-13
00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:08.279
settings for one assessment and apply them
to all the others, except for the

cue-14
00:01:08.279 --> 00:01:13.839
available date and due date. For example,
here I changed the number of attempts and

cue-15
00:01:13.839 --> 00:01:19.219
late policy of the Getting Started
assessment. All I need to do is to select

cue-16
00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:25.839
it from the list, click bulk apply, and
confirm. This applies your

cue-17
00:01:25.839 --> 00:01:30.720
selected setting to all assessment at
once. Really time-saving, right? There

cue-18
00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:35.160
will be another video explaining student
progress and insights. If you have

cue-19
00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:38.719
additional questions, visit our OLI help
page.
